  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HAY - Strengthening the participation and influence of Yanomami Woman</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to strengthen HAY&apos;s communication strategy of radio installation in isolated communities living in Yanomami indigenous territory, and to strengthen the participation of indigenous women to access their rights.

Despite the fact that the Yanomami people were granted the right to their territory in 1982, illegal gold miners continue to enter their territory, creating violence, disease, and polluting rivers from mercury used in the extraction of gold. Communities are also facing a health crisis in service provision. Both of these challenges adversely affect women. 

Activities include: a) provide women&apos;s right training to 60 Yanomami women and girls in order to strengthen their participation and influence on public policies related to their rights to health and land protection; b) promote gender awareness in their communities; and c) installation of a radio and a women&apos;s rights awareness workshop in the Komomassipetheri community of 110 people as a form of constant communication with HAY on external threats.</narrative>
  </description>
